&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;x_MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Our ambition is to attract the very best diverse talent to Ogilvy, and to be the employer of choice in the UK. We want everyone to feel welcome when they join us, and once they’re here, for them to want to stay with us, grow their career, and to feel they belong with us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_MsoNoSpacing&quot;&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer and we’re committed to creating an inclusive, welcoming environment for everyone who wants to work at Ogilvy. For us, diversity, equity and inclusion is integrated into everything that we do. We believe that for creativity to flourish, everything about how we work must have diversity at its core. Your race, colour, ethnic, religion, gender, gender identity, national origin, sexual orientation, age, marital status, disability, have no bearing on our hiring decisions, but we encourage everyone to feel free to express their true selves in an environment we are consistently striving to make as inclusive as possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_MsoNoSpacing&quot;&gt;We aim to facilitate an accessible and positive application experience for all candidates. If you require any adjustments from us to support you through the process or expect to require any adjustments to working conditions to be able to best perform in the role, please let us know. We are happy to consider all reasonable adjustments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_MsoNoSpacing&quot;&gt;If you live with a disability and you would like to take advantage of our offer of a guaranteed interview under the Disability Confident Scheme, please ensure you fill out our voluntary Equal Opportunities Questionnaire when applying.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are PMG&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;PMG, a global independent platform company engineered for impact, integrates business strategy, media, creative, and data within a single operating model powered by our proprietary operating system, Alli. With more than 1,000 employees, PMG partners with brands including Apple, Nike, Dropbox, Experian, Sephora, and Whole Foods. Our work has earned top industry honors, including Cannes Lions and Adweek’s Media Plan of the Year, and PMG has won 40+ workplace culture awards, including being the only company to rank among Ad Age’s Best Places to Work for 11 consecutive years.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id=&quot;message-list&quot;&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;message-list&quot;&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;message-list_1788204638.133349&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You&#39;ll Be Working With&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At PMG, our Influencer &amp;amp; Branded Content team is at the intersection of culture, storytelling, and strategy, helping brands connect with audiences in authentic, meaningful ways. We craft high-impact influencer campaigns that go beyond traditional advertising, driving engagement, building brand affinity, and delivering measurable results across social, digital, and experiential platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Influencer &amp;amp; Branded Content Senior Manager, you’ll play a key leadership role in shaping and delivering influencer and creator strategies across PMG’s clients. You’ll collaborate with creators, talent agencies, media strategists, content teams, client leaders, and brand partners to develop programs that connect cultural relevance with business impact. You’ll help strengthen PMG’s influencer and creator marketing capabilities by establishing scalable best practices, developing strong talent and platform relationships, and ensuring a high standard of strategy, execution, measurement, and client service.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll help advance the future of branded content at PMG by identifying emerging creator trends, exploring new content formats and platforms, and translating innovation into actionable opportunities for clients. You’ll also lead and develop team members, helping them strengthen their strategic thinking, channel expertise, and ability to deliver exceptional work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re passionate about shaping culture through creator-driven storytelling, using data to guide meaningful decisions, and building innovative influencer programs that deliver measurable impact, this is the place to make your mark.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead full-scale influencer and branded content campaigns from brief to delivery—including strategy development, talent identification, negotiations, publisher partnerships, content approvals, and reporting—translating business objectives, audience insights, and cultural trends into impactful creator programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee campaign strategy and execution in partnership with internal team members, ensuring every detail is delivered with excellence, on time, aligned with brand standards and client business objectives, and optimized for measurable success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and mentor a team of professionals, supporting workload planning, day-to-day execution, coaching, feedback, performance management, and long-term professional development while building a culture of collaboration, creativity, and accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Director of Influencer &amp;amp; Branded Content to help evolve PMG’s offerings, develop scalable frameworks, best practices, processes, and measurement approaches, and train team members to grow their expertise and impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a senior subject matter expert in influencer marketing and branded content, bringing a strong point of view to client conversations, strategic recommendations, new business opportunities, and emerging creator trends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a senior point of contact for clients, clearly communicating strategic plans, campaign updates, recommendations, and results through regular calls, emails, and in-person meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop innovative influencer and branded content programs for existing clients and new business opportunities, partnering closely with account, strategy, media, and creative teams to connect creator ideas to broader marketing objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Play an active role in new business efforts, contributing to RFPs, pitch development, influencer research, and presentation storytelling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain strong relationships with creators, talent agencies, publishers, and platform partners to expand access to talent, industry insights, platform innovation, and strategic opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring platform fluency across both established and emerging social channels, shaping creator strategies that are native to each platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and distill influencer marketing trends into practical strategies that keep our work relevant, fresh, and forward-thinking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply and evolve measurement frameworks to evaluate creator performance, campaign effectiveness, audience engagement, and business impact, translating results into actionable recommendations for clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic guidance and quality oversight across campaign planning, creator selection, contracting, content approvals, reporting, compliance, and partnership deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with senior leaders to identify opportunities to improve team processes, resource planning, capabilities, and approaches that support continued client and business growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI, automation, and technology to elevate the quality and efficiency of work, streamline processes, and enable faster, more informed decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The primary focus of this role is the Influencer &amp;amp; Branded Content channel, ensuring excellence in strategy, execution, and performance. However, responsibilities may extend across other media channels as needed to support broader campaign objectives and business priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in Influencer &amp;amp; Branded Content, including 3+ years of leadership experience, with a bachelor’s degree or equivalent work experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring advanced expertise in content creation and influencer marketing strategy, developing creator-led programs that connect cultural insight, platform behavior, audience needs, and client business goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong experience in contract review and proposal development, navigating creator and partnership negotiations with clarity, consistency, and a focus on delivering value for clients and partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring exceptional attention to detail, maintaining high standards across campaign execution, reporting, content approvals, compliance, and partnership deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong proficiency in project implementation, leading complex influencer and branded content programs from strategic planning through launch, optimization, and post-campaign learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are skilled in presentation and communication, delivering clear strategic narratives, senior-level recommendations, and performance insights to clients, partners, and internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a deep understanding of advertising standards, client service, and relationship management, helping brands and creators build trusted partnerships that meet business, legal, and platform expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are proficient with influencer management dashboards, social media platforms, and the broader social media ecosystem, using data to evaluate creators, guide recommendations, and improve campaign performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience building relationships across the influencer marketing ecosystem, including creators, talent agencies, publishers, and platform partners, and leveraging those relationships to strengthen client programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring strategic thinking, business and financial acumen, and thoughtful resource management to guide account priorities, team planning, and scalable approaches to client growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have demonstrated experience managing and developing team members, balancing day-to-day leadership with coaching, feedback, performance management, and long-term professional development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A commitment to curiosity and adaptability as a Continual Learner, staying at the forefront of media innovation while prioritizing client success with a Customer-Focused mindset that seeks opportunities to deliver meaningful value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A dedication to People-Focused leadership, fostering collaboration, innovation, and professional growth by Leading by Example and nurturing strong relationships that empower others to excel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance-Based Rewards:&lt;/strong&gt; Your impact should be part of your reward. This role is eligible for PMG’s annual bonus program—a standout part of our total compensation offering and an opportunity to share in our success. Bonus awards are informed by individual impact and performance, as well as team and company results, and are subject to applicable program terms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Professional Development: &lt;/strong&gt;Keep growing through learning and development programs, mentorship opportunities, and support for career advancement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generous Time Off: &lt;/strong&gt;Take the time you need to recharge, connect with loved ones, and enjoy life outside work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Parental Leave: &lt;/strong&gt;Receive paid parental leave during life’s important family moments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Retirement Benefits: &lt;/strong&gt;Build for your future with competitive retirement benefits, including employer contributions or matching where applicable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fertility and Family Support: &lt;/strong&gt;Access fertility and family-building benefits for eligible employees and their spouses or partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Healthcare: &lt;/strong&gt;Choose from medical, dental, and vision coverage designed to support you and your family.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pet Insurance: &lt;/strong&gt;Access optional coverage for the four-legged members of your family.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lifestyle Spending Account: &lt;/strong&gt;Receive company-funded support for eligible health and well-being expenses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commuter Benefits: &lt;/strong&gt;Access support for your commute where available.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Volunteering Opportunities: &lt;/strong&gt;Receive eight paid hours each year to give back to your community.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Tools and Training: &lt;/strong&gt;Access enterprise AI tools and ongoing training that helps PMGers use AI effectively, creatively, and responsibly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Our benefits and compensation programs may vary by location and eligibility and are subject to applicable plan terms. We’ll share full details during the hiring process.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Sets Us Apart&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Being part of PMG means joining a company culture that’s unmatched in digital. We&#39;re dedicated to working hard to serve our employees and clients, delivering value, results, and innovation—which often requires true grit and agility. We believe in taking care of ourselves and each other to continuously improve in every way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In alignment with our core values to be inclusive and always change for the better, PMG is committed to creating a more diverse and inclusive culture, and we are proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We believe that we only change for the better by bringing diverse perspectives to our company. PMG recruits, employs, trains, compensates, and promotes regardless of race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

